# 2. THE HANDED LIST WAS ONCE MISSING gen_tb_top.sv, and with it every run of every test would have died in
#    build_phase at time 0 on "misc vif not in uvm_config_db" (gen_fcov_pkg.sv:705). That file carries one
#    line, the uvm_config_db::set that publishes misc_vif. NO STATIC CHECK CAN SEE THAT: hashes, the
#    manifest, codegen --check, the codegen unit test, unbuilt-mark and a full TB compile all pass without
#    it, because a config_db lookup is a run-time fact. The smokes above are therefore run from a tree
#    assembled STRICTLY from the handed list rather than from a working root, which is the check that
#    found it.
# ================================================================================================
# SAMPLE EVENT, SIGNAL SOURCE AND FIELD CAVEATS, PER COVERGROUP (LOG-096)
#
# CG-IRQ-001 gen_irq_entry_cg. EVENT: one per retired record with rvfi_intr. SOURCE: the record itself and
#   the model of record the scoreboard publishes (mcause's cause, mstatus, mepc, mie as of that record),
#   plus the pin levels kept from the irq agent's own events. CAVEATS: mstatus is the state AFTER the entry,
#   so cp_mie_global reads MPIE, which holds MIE as it was; cp_u_path and cp_u_pending_at_return are passed
#   -1 until CG-IRQ-005's handler stack lands, which is a deferral and not a claim.
#
# CG-IRQ-003 gen_irq_pending_model_cg. EVENTS: three, not one per record. ev_edge is a CYCLE event (a pin
#   change from the agent's event, or the commit of a retired mie write); ev_access is a retired CSR access
#   to mip or mie; ev_mie is a retired mstatus write that changes MIE, or ANY retired mret. Each entry point
#   fills its own coverpoints and passes -1 for the rest.
#   SOURCE: the irq checker's own published per-cycle sampled view (gen_tb_pkg::gen_irq_view), written by
#   gen_irq_checker at its sample point, so this covergroup judges a record's commit cycle from the SAME
#   sample the checker judges it from and no offset arithmetic lives here. The checker now reads its mie
#   history from that same holder, so there is ONE history and not two that agree by inspection.
#   CAVEATS: the pin EDGE itself comes from the agent's event, because the checker's sample at that cycle
#   holds the value BEFORE the driver's falling-edge change and cannot express "a pin changed here". A
#   record whose commit cycle has aged out of the published window samples NOTHING and is counted as a view
#   miss in the report line. cp_state at a pin event is the last retired record's state except sleep, which
#   is read from core_busy at that cycle (mubi-off is the controller's WAIT_SLEEP/SLEEP). cp_mie_write reads
#   the value the instruction PRESENTED, not what the WARL mask kept. An edge whose class the plan does not
#   name samples nothing rather than a bin it did not earn.
#
# CG-IRQ-010 gen_irq_debug_interplay_cg. EVENT: one per WINDOW, sampled after the record that decides
#   cp_post_exit. A window opens on a record with a line pending while in debug mode or stepping outside it,
#   and closes at its exit (a dret, or the stepped record itself). SOURCE: the model of record for
#   debug_mode, dcsr, is_dret, is_mret, is_intr, nmi_pend and nmi_int_pend; the published view for the pins;
#   the locally tracked NMI mode for cp_mode.debug_in_nmi_handler.
#   CAVEATS: a record can BOTH open and close a window (a line that becomes pending on the dret itself, or
#   the single record of a step window), which the first version got wrong and the smoke caught: a window
#   opened on the dret waited for a second dret that never came and nothing was ever sampled. A window whose
#   observation has not closed is DROPPED and counted ("dropped unclosed"), never sampled, as the plan says.
#   KNOWN DIVERGENCE FROM THE PLAN TEXT, already with the DV Lead and deferred by it to one consolidated
#   touch: the plan qualifies both cp_post_exit bins by dpc, but a step window's next retirement is in the
#   debug ROM at an address BELOW the program's, so a dpc comparison cannot discriminate there; the sampler
#   classifies on the first record after the exit, which decides the same question directly.
#
# CG-IRQ-011 gen_irq_reset_fetch_en_cg. EVENTS: two. ev_reset is the reset release, with the pins latched
#   there, the first architectural event, the first reset-time CSR read-backs and a boot mret, each its own
#   sample so one coverpoint carries one fact. ev_off is a CLOSED fetch-enable Off window of at least the
#   plan's 20 cycles, TAKEN from gen_misc_monitor's published queue rather than detected here a second time
#   from the same pin, and completed by the first fetch after the return to On, which arrives on the ibus
#   subscription this class already had.
#   CAVEATS: cp_fetch_off is judged from the published samples that still cover the window, so a window
#   longer than the published depth is judged on the part still covered. cp_fetch_on_after compares the
#   fetched address against mtvec as of the last record, read through the ISA shim, which returns the value
#   BEFORE that record; mtvec rarely moves, and a run that moved it inside an Off window would classify from
#   the older base. A debug request at reset with neither an NMI nor a regular line has no bin in the plan
#   and samples nothing.
#
# BINS NO STIMULUS IN THE TREE REACHES TODAY, for the entry that declares them rather than for this landing:
#   CG-IRQ-003 cp_state.u_mode / step / sleep / debug_mode / nmi_mode, cp_transition.nmi_only_rise, every
#   cp_mip_access bin, cp_mie_write.all_ones / fast_only / random_masked, cp_mie_global_edge.mret_mpie0_pending.
#   CG-IRQ-010 the whole group needs a debug request or dcsr.step together with a raised line; only the
#   dbgstorm fixture above does that, and no testlist entry does.
#   CG-IRQ-011 every cp_fetch_off bin but the one the fetchen fixture hits, and cp_boot_mret.to_u_mie1,
#   which needs a U-mode boot program.
